WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.380
Ask people about the future,

00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:05.060
and you'll hear a lot of maybes.

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:08.870
Dr Ingrid Vasseur convenes Futures in Committee,

00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:12.503
the seminar series of the School of Emergent Priorities.

00:00:12.603 --> 00:00:14.743
I follow those maybes into the committee room,

00:00:14.943 --> 00:00:16.333
to see which ones survive.

00:00:16.833 --> 00:00:19.503
We matched ninety-six scan entries to their minutes.

00:00:20.003 --> 00:00:22.053
A typical entry had five maybes.

00:00:22.253 --> 00:00:23.785
By the time it was minuted,

00:00:23.785 --> 00:00:24.636
none were left.

00:00:25.335 --> 00:00:27.395
Eight hundred and ninety-five citations,

00:00:27.596 --> 00:00:30.846
and an h-index of twenty-five.

00:00:30.946 --> 00:00:33.666
No one at Slop University has got there with fewer outputs.

00:00:33.966 --> 00:00:35.976
She needed just a hundred and fifty-nine.

00:00:36.876 --> 00:00:38.586
Every decision starts as a maybe.

00:00:38.886 --> 00:00:39.444
I want to know

00:00:39.594 --> 00:00:40.644
where the maybe goes.

00:00:41.644 --> 00:00:42.897
Read her work on our website,

00:00:43.047 --> 00:00:44.557
and find us on Bluesky.
